# Product Detail Page 7-Test Strategy Sprint

**Date:** 2026-04-02
**Target State:** Complete 7-test coverage for product detail page proving robust, professional architecture and functionality
**Estimated Duration:** 2 days

---

## Sprint Metadata

### Scope Lock Rules
- **NO** globals.css changes
- **NO** homepage changes
- **NO** data structure changes
- **NO** modifications outside product detail page scope
- **NO** new dependencies without approval

### Pre-Work Lessons Applied
- **Critical**: Tailwind breakpoint shadowing (use lg-desktop: not lg:)
- **Critical**: GROQ schema assumptions (verify field types)
- **High**: Type consolidation (export from data layer)
- **High**: Server-driven filtering (no client-side filtering)
- **High**: Pre-flight baseline check required

---

## Research & Audit Context

### Current Architecture
```
app/(store)/product/[slug]/page.tsx (Server Component)
├── getProductBySlug() (Data Layer)
├── ProductDetail (Client Component)
│   ├── ImageGallery (Client Component)
│   ├── ProductInfo (Client Component)
│   │   ├── Price (Client Component)
│   │   └── QuantitySelector (Client Component)
│   └── RelatedProducts (Client Component)
```

### Design System Tokens Available
- `type-section-hed`, `type-price`, `type-overline`
- `btn-primary`, `btn-cart` (unused)
- `surface-productImage`, `text-accent-500`
- Custom breakpoints: `lg-desktop:`, `lg-touch:`

---

## Scope Contracts

### SC1: Architecture Integrity Test (Test 0)
**Gap Coverage:** Foundation validation
**Target State:** Prove architecture is simple, robust, professional

#### DoD (Sequenced)
- [ ] Pass 1: Create test file structure (tests/e2e/architecture.spec.ts)
- [ ] Pass 2: Implement 5 architecture assertions (circular deps, data independence, interface stability, unidirectional flow, error isolation)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 2: Desktop test execution (1280px)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 4: Desktop interaction (test execution)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 2: Mobile test execution (375px)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 4: Mobile interaction (test execution)

#### Delegation
**Execution:** `/implement "architecture integrity test with 5 assertions"`
**Build:** `/build architecture-test Pass1` → `/build architecture-test Pass2` → `/build architecture-test Pass3-L2` → `/build architecture-test Pass3-L4`
**Verify:** `/test` after Pass 3 completion

---

### SC2: Page Load & Data Integrity Test (Test 1)
**Gap Coverage:** Core functionality validation
**Target State:** Verify page loads correctly with all data displaying

#### DoD (Sequenced)
- [ ] Pass 1: Test page navigation and 404 handling
- [ ] Pass 2: Test data fetching and display (name, brand, price, stock)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 2: Desktop layout verification (1280px)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 3: Desktop surface (visual verification)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 4: Desktop interaction (data display)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 2: Mobile layout verification (375px)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 3: Mobile surface (touch interaction)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 4: Mobile interaction (data display)

#### Delegation
**Execution:** `/implement "page load and data integrity test"`
**Build:** `/build page-load-test Pass1` → `/build page-load-test Pass2` → `/build page-load-test Pass3-L2` → `/build page-load-test Pass3-L4`
**Verify:** `/test` after each Pass 3 Layer

---

### SC3: Add to Cart Button Test (Test 2)
**Gap Coverage:** Component interface validation
**Target State:** Verify add to cart button wires data correctly to external callback

#### Hard Boundary Constraints
- **IN SCOPE**: Button click, data preparation, callback invocation
- **OUT OF SCOPE**: Basket functionality, cart state management, checkout flow
- **BOUNDARY**: Component stops at addItem() callback invocation
- **NO TESTING**: What happens to data after callback
- **NO TESTING**: Cart UI updates, basket page, checkout process

#### DoD (Sequenced)
- [ ] Pass 1: Test button exists and is enabled/disabled correctly
- [ ] Pass 2: Test button click with correct data payload (product ID, name, price, quantity, image, brand)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 2: Desktop button interaction (1280px)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 4: Desktop interaction (click, verify addItem called with correct data)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 2: Mobile button interaction (375px)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 4: Mobile interaction (touch, verify addItem called)

#### Verification Requirements
- **MUST**: Mock addItem function (jest.fn())
- **MUST**: Verify addItem called exactly once with correct data structure
- **MUST NOT**: Test what addItem does with the data
- **MUST NOT**: Test cart state changes
- **MUST NOT**: Test any basket/store functionality

#### Delegation
**Execution:** `/implement "add to cart button component interface test"`
**Build:** `/build add-cart-button-test Pass1` → `/build add-cart-button-test Pass2` → `/build add-cart-button-test Pass3-L4`
**Verify:** `/test` after Pass 3 completion

---

### SC4: Navigation Links Test (Test 3)
**Gap Coverage:** Link integrity validation
**Target State:** Verify all links on product page navigate to valid destinations

#### Hard Boundary Constraints
- **IN SCOPE**: Link clicks, URL navigation, destination page loads
- **OUT OF SCOPE**: Destination page functionality, external site behavior
- **BOUNDARY**: Test stops at destination page load verification
- **NO TESTING**: What happens on destination pages
- **NO TESTING**: External site functionality, third-party behavior

#### DoD (Sequenced)
- [ ] Pass 1: Test breadcrumb links navigate to correct URLs
- [ ] Pass 2: Test related products links navigate to product pages (load verification only)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 2: Desktop link navigation (1280px)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 4: Desktop interaction (click links, verify URL changes, verify page loads)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 2: Mobile link navigation (375px)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 4: Mobile interaction (touch links, verify URL changes, verify page loads)

#### Verification Requirements
- **MUST**: Test link href attributes are correct
- **MUST**: Test navigation results in correct URL
- **MUST**: Test destination page loads (no 404)
- **MUST NOT**: Test functionality on destination pages
- **MUST NOT**: Test external site behavior
- **MUST NOT**: Test what happens after navigation

#### Delegation
**Execution:** `/implement "navigation links component interface test"`
**Build:** `/build navigation-links-test Pass1` → `/build navigation-links-test Pass2` → `/build navigation-links-test Pass3-L4`
**Verify:** `/test` after Pass 3 completion

---

### SC5: Responsive Layout Test (Test 4)
**Gap Coverage:** Component layout adaptation validation
**Target State:** Verify product detail components adapt correctly to viewports

#### Hard Boundary Constraints
- **IN SCOPE**: Component layout changes, element visibility, touch target sizes
- **OUT OF SCOPE**: Browser behavior, OS interactions, external responsive behavior
- **BOUNDARY**: Test stops at component DOM adaptation verification
- **NO TESTING**: Browser window resizing behavior
- **NO TESTING**: OS-level responsive features

#### DoD (Sequenced)
- [ ] Pass 1: Test component layout changes at critical breakpoints (375px, 768px, 1920px)
- [ ] Pass 2: Test component visibility and positioning changes
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 2: Mobile component layout (375px)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 3: Mobile surface (component visual regression)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 4: Mobile interaction (component touch targets)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 2: Desktop component layout (1920px)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 3: Desktop surface (component visual regression)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 4: Desktop interaction (component hover states)

#### Verification Requirements
- **MUST**: Test component DOM structure changes at breakpoints
- **MUST**: Test component visibility and positioning
- **MUST**: Test component touch targets meet minimum size
- **MUST NOT**: Test browser window behavior
- **MUST NOT**: Test OS-level responsive features
- **MUST NOT**: Test external system responsive behavior

#### Delegation
**Execution:** `/implement "responsive component layout test"`
**Build:** `/build responsive-layout-test Pass1` → `/build responsive-layout-test Pass2` → `/build responsive-layout-test Pass3-L4`
**Verify:** `/test` with component screenshots after each Layer

---

### SC6: Edge Case Data Test (Test 5)
**Gap Coverage:** Component data handling validation
**Target State:** Verify product detail components handle problematic data gracefully

#### Hard Boundary Constraints
- **IN SCOPE**: Component data display, null/undefined handling, error boundaries
- **OUT OF SCOPE**: Data source validation, server error handling, external data issues
- **BOUNDARY**: Test stops at component data rendering verification
- **NO TESTING**: Data fetching errors, server responses, external data sources
- **NO TESTING**: Database validation, API error handling

#### DoD (Sequenced)
- [ ] Pass 1: Test component display with null brand, out of stock, no images data
- [ ] Pass 2: Test component behavior with very long names, special characters, malformed data
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 2: Desktop component error handling (1280px)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 4: Desktop interaction (component graceful degradation)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 2: Mobile component error handling (375px)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 4: Mobile interaction (component error boundaries)

#### Verification Requirements
- **MUST**: Test component renders correctly with null/undefined data
- **MUST**: Test component handles malformed data without crashing
- **MUST**: Test component displays fallbacks for missing data
- **MUST NOT**: Test data source validation
- **MUST NOT**: Test server error handling
- **MUST NOT**: Test external data source reliability

#### Delegation
**Execution:** `/implement "edge case component data handling test"`
**Build:** `/build edge-case-data-test Pass1` → `/build edge-case-data-test Pass2` → `/build edge-case-data-test Pass3-L4`
**Verify:** `/test` after Pass 3 completion

---

### SC7: Invalid Route Handling Test (Test 6)
**Gap Coverage**: Route error handling validation
**Target State**: Verify product detail page handles invalid routes gracefully

#### Hard Boundary Constraints
- **IN SCOPE**: Route resolution, 404 page display, error component rendering
- **OUT OF SCOPE**: Server routing, external redirects, DNS resolution
- **BOUNDARY**: Test stops at error page component verification
- **NO TESTING**: Server configuration, external routing, network issues
- **NO TESTING**: DNS resolution, load balancer behavior, CDN routing

#### DoD (Sequenced)
- [ ] Pass 1: Test non-existent product routes display 404 component
- [ ] Pass 2: Test malformed URLs and special characters are handled by routing
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 2: Desktop error component display (1280px)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 4: Desktop interaction (error component navigation)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 2: Mobile error component display (375px)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 4: Mobile interaction (error component navigation)

#### Verification Requirements
- **MUST**: Test route resolution fails gracefully
- **MUST**: Test 404 component displays correctly
- **MUST**: Test error component provides navigation options
- **MUST NOT**: Test server routing configuration
- **MUST NOT**: Test external routing systems
- **MUST NOT**: Test network-level error handling

#### Delegation
**Execution:** `/implement "invalid route component handling test"`
**Build:** `/build invalid-route-test Pass1` → `/build invalid-route-test Pass2` → `/build invalid-route-test Pass3-L4`
**Verify:** `/test` after Pass 3 completion
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 2: Desktop error pages (1280px)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 4: Desktop interaction (error navigation)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 2: Mobile error pages (375px)
- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 4: Mobile interaction (error navigation)

#### Delegation
**Execution:** `/implement "invalid routes handling test"`
**Build:** `/build invalid-routes-test Pass1` → `/build invalid-routes-test Pass2` → `/build invalid-routes-test Pass3-L4`
**Verify:** `/test` after Pass 3 completion

