## RWD Strategy

| Component | Desktop (1280px) | Mobile (375px) | Implementation |
|-----------|------------------|----------------|----------------|
| Test Execution | Full browser automation | Mobile viewport | Playwright projects |
| Visual Checks | Screenshot comparison | Screenshot comparison |toHaveScreenshot() |
| Interactions | Mouse events | Touch events | touch/pointer events |

---

## Files at Risk of Regression

| File | Risk | Mitigation |
|------|------|------------|
| `getProductBySlug.ts` | Brand data structure changes | Test 1 & 5 verify component data handling |
| `ProductInfo.tsx` | Add to cart logic changes | Test 2 verifies component interface only |
| `page.tsx` | Metadata generation changes | Test 1 verifies page load component |
| `ImageGallery.tsx` | Zoom modal changes | Test 3 verifies navigation links only |
| `tailwind.config.ts` | Token additions affect styling | Test 4 verifies component responsive layout |

---

## Pre-Sprint Baseline

### Action Required: `/test` for baseline capture
- Scope: Current product detail page functionality
- DoDs: Existing page load, add to cart, navigation
- Output: BASELINE CAPTURED before sprint work

**Execute Before Sprint Start:**
```bash
npm run build
npx playwright test --grep "product detail" --baseline
```

---

## Delegation Commands

### Sprint Execution Sequence
```bash
# 1. Architecture foundation (Test 0)
/implement "architecture integrity test with 5 assertions"

# 2. Core functionality (Tests 1-3)
/implement "page load and data integrity test"
/implement "add to cart functionality test"
/implement "navigation and link integrity test"

# 3. Responsive and edge cases (Tests 4-6)
/implement "responsive design test with visual regression"
/implement "edge case data handling test"
/implement "invalid routes handling test"
```

### Verification Commands
```bash
# After each SC completion
npx playwright test tests/e2e/architecture.spec.ts
npx playwright test tests/e2e/product-detail.spec.ts

# Final sprint verification
npx playwright test tests/e2e/
npm run build
```

